Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.41,0:00:03.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Agent of God, you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.53,0:00:06.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, try passing judgment upon me.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.74,0:00:09.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For I am the Strong Arm Alchemist,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.71,0:00:12.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alex Louis Armstrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.00,0:00:15.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Allow me to show you\Nthe artistic alchemy
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.67,0:00:20.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that has been passed down among\Nthe Armstrong family for generations!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.14,0:00:27.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Another shot!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.86,0:00:38.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The opposite of destruction is creation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.90,0:00:41.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The opposite of creation is destruction.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.45,0:00:43.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Destroy and create.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.20,0:00:45.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the law of the universe!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.12,0:00:52.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll deal with you after I kill Fullmetal and Crystal.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.13,0:01:03.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A combination of physical strength and alchemy, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.38,0:01:04.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This could be trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.39,0:01:07.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brown skin and red eyes...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.31,0:01:09.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold it!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.48,0:01:21.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The god of your people strictly forbids alchemy, does he not?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.20,0:01:29.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The transmutation process of alchemy \Ncan be broadly divided into comprehension,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.20,0:01:29.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,decomposition, and reconstruction.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.91,0:01:34.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You stop your transmutation process at the second one, decomposition.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.79,0:01:37.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It is still unmistakably alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.71,0:01:40.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I do only as this arm instructs me to.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.30,0:01:43.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if it is contrary to God's will!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.85,0:01:59.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything\Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.57,0:02:04.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything,\Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.86,0:02:09.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's\NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.62,0:02:15.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that\Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.94,0:04:07.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, now what do we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.44,0:04:11.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whatever we do, I'd like to stay as far away as possible from that guy in the sunglasses.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.37,0:04:17.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.67,0:04:30.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, do you have a back door?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.43,0:04:37.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're not going back to the Eastern Command Center?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.02,0:04:40.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Since Brigadier General Grand showed up,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.18,0:04:44.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it could mean that there are reasons keeping even the Colonel from protecting Doctor Marcoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.90,0:04:48.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right.\NTo make matters worse, there are all those people from Central here now as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.57,0:04:51.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are other people\Nhere from Central?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.41,0:04:53.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer and his entourage.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.53,0:04:56.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To catch me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.41,0:04:58.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, that's not why.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.00,0:05:02.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, okay, here we go!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.83,0:05:06.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on! Hold on!\NHey, hold on!\NOkay, I'm gonna get you!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.34,0:05:16.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've had enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.10,0:05:21.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't care if I do\Nget killed by that man.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.69,0:05:26.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He has the right to do so.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.20,0:05:41.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel! We found him!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.08,0:05:45.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.00,0:05:47.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, Major! What happened?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.96,0:05:49.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whoa!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.59,0:05:50.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was close...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.34,0:05:56.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is intense.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.59,0:05:58.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel, what about Brig. Gen. Grand?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.56,0:06:03.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If he's alive after that,\Nthen the Iron Blood Alchemist
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.68,0:06:06.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,can come back to life after\Nbeing turned into hamburger.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.19,0:06:10.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But he was an expert in military hand-to-hand combat, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.74,0:06:20.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was Scar, without a doubt.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.12,0:06:23.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.08,0:06:26.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's an Ishbalan.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.12,0:06:28.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major, don't get up!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.75,0:06:31.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm terribly sorry I could not\Ncarry out your orders, Lt.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.75,0:06:34.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel.\NI saw him... his skin...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.22,0:06:37.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,his eyes...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.47,0:06:40.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those are definitely the traits of the Ishbalan people.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.93,0:06:46.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see. So that's why he's going after State Alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.44,0:06:53.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If he's of the Ishbalan people, \Nthen why do you have to be killed by him?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.65,0:06:57.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Ishbalans instigated \Na war of independence, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.41,0:07:02.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There were a lot of them who died,\Nbut the military also suffered many casualties.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.08,0:07:10.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If everyone who ever lost in a war \Nswore revenge, there'd be no end to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.58,0:07:13.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was no war.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.05,0:07:15.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was a massacre.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.85,0:07:25.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The people of Ishbal were \Na tribe in the Eastern Region
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.47,0:07:27.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,who believed in Ishbala \Nas the one and only creator.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.19,0:07:31.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They held religious values\Nthat were different from ours.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.61,0:07:37.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We think of the world's composition\Nas something which can be mathematically determined
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.49,0:07:40.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and have high regard for the\Nequivalent exchange of alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.70,0:07:48.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But the Ishbalans thought of alchemy as the work of the devil,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.03,0:07:48.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,which perverts the world\Nthat was given to us by God.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.33,0:07:56.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As a result, there were resistance movements that sprang up from time to time.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.46,0:07:57.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And then, thirteen years ago...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.38,0:08:01.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, what do you think you're doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.68,0:08:08.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...while an officer was\Nconducting an inspection,\Nhe accidentally shot a child.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.10,0:08:15.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That incident lead to the outbreak of large-scale uprisings and riots.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.32,0:08:30.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Before long, the rebellion had spread throughout the whole Eastern Region\Nand had become a war\Nthat lasted seven years.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.37,0:08:34.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then, in the final days of fighting...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.30,0:08:41.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the higher-ups decided to employ State Alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.01,0:08:45.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.22,0:08:49.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because of their doctrines, the Ishbalans have neither alchemy nor up-to-date weapons!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.56,0:08:52.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you hope to obtain by further antagonizing them?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.94,0:08:54.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Have you brought them?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.81,0:08:58.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're still under research.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.28,0:09:00.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides, there's no need to use them.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.40,0:09:03.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As a matter of fact,\Nthe rebellion is steadily spreading.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.41,0:09:08.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's because you're trying to keep them down by force,\Nand so, more and more tribes are cooperating with the enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.83,0:09:14.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you saying that what\Nthe Führer is doing is wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.30,0:09:22.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We already have several thousand soldiers
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.38,0:09:26.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and several tens of thousands of civilians who have become casualties.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.68,0:09:28.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is war.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.14,0:09:32.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Crystal Alchemist, let me see them.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.87,0:09:54.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}In order to hasten the end\Nof this war, as of tomorrow,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.87,0:09:59.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}I'm authorizing the use of\Nalchemic augmentation agents!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.55,0:10:06.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}So, then what happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.55,0:10:07.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.59,0:10:08.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.97,0:10:12.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For every battlefield\Nthe State Alchemists were dispatched to,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.73,0:10:16.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it was all over in one night.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.89,0:10:57.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There he is!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.35,0:10:59.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Over here!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.09,0:11:22.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yow!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.46,0:11:26.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ow!\NLet me see.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.60,0:11:34.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On the battlefield,\NI came across this couple.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.85,0:11:39.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They were doctors,\Nand would treat people, regardless of\Nwhether they were friend or foe.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.73,0:11:41.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.24,0:11:48.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.28,0:11:52.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was incredible, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.83,0:11:57.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, they died.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.30,0:12:07.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel Grand, what's going on?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.38,0:12:10.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This place has become a contact point for Ishbalan refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.01,0:12:12.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The doctors were\Nin cahoots with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.55,0:12:16.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They just wanted to save as many lives as they could, that's all!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.81,0:12:20.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The lives they save\Nare killing my men.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.79,0:12:41.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.29,0:12:48.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You were just following orders.\NThe sin is upon me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.46,0:12:52.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As fellow doctors, they saved lives...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.22,0:12:53.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,whereas I...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.68,0:12:57.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.43,0:13:02.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Would you keep quiet and let me run away?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.40,0:13:06.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And so, I left with\Nthe Philosopher's Stones
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.82,0:13:09.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and all of the materials\Nrelating to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.99,0:13:12.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But it was too late.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.70,0:13:18.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The people of Ishbal\Nhad been exterminated.\NI heard that there were only a handful of survivors.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.70,0:13:22.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even so, that's no reason for you to be killed!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.58,0:13:26.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He has a legitimate reason\Nfor his revenge.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.46,0:13:30.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can there be any legitimacy to his revenge\Nwhen he drags people who aren't involved into it?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.09,0:13:33.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What he's doing...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.34,0:13:37.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is wrapping his ugly lust for vengeance up inside a claim of being God's agent
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.14,0:13:38.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and acting like\Nit's all noble. That's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.72,0:13:42.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still...\NBrother, if you had been...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.02,0:13:45.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I would do the same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.69,0:13:47.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's the Principle of\NEquivalent Exchange, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.77,0:13:48.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.94,0:13:51.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Taking revenge won't ever bring anything back!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.82,0:13:54.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All you'd need to do is live.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.95,0:13:57.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Live... Live, and find happiness.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.83,0:14:07.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.84,0:14:19.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san,\Nwhy don't you come\Nhide in our hometown?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.35,0:14:21.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It won't even take three days by train to get there.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.47,0:14:22.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.64,0:14:24.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It'll be a little hard on us going back, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.10,0:14:28.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a house there, where an Automail craftswoman named Rockbell lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.73,0:14:30.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure they'd let us...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.98,0:14:33.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rockbell...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.78,0:14:36.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't go there... Not me...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.82,0:14:39.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.62,0:14:47.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What foolishness!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.79,0:14:51.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You would rely upon weapons that have been enhanced by the curse of alchemy?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.00,0:14:52.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case...!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.39,0:15:04.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's far enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.73,0:15:05.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel Mustang!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.02,0:15:09.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mustang?\NThe State Alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.52,0:15:11.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Indeed I am.\NColonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.65,0:15:15.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am the Flame Alchemist,\NRoy Mustang.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.49,0:15:21.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yet another who deviates from the path of God?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.20,0:15:24.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You would still challenge me to battle, knowing that I am the Flame Alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.91,0:15:26.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.08,0:15:30.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.92,0:15:37.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why'd you do that\Nall of a sudden?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.72,0:15:41.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're good for nothing on rainy days, so please stay back, Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.68,0:15:44.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't make sparks\Nwhen it's this damp, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.14,0:15:47.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.23,0:15:54.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He sure is fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.52,0:15:55.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After him!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.73,0:15:58.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Breda, you wait for Fullmetal at the train station.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.57,0:16:00.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why would Ed be going to the train station?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.95,0:16:04.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's obvious that he's thinking about getting Marcoh out of here.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.25,0:16:12.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.92,0:16:14.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait up!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.25,0:16:16.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We aren't going to take your research from you by force.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.26,0:16:20.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No! I can't go!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.19,0:16:37.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This time, I know that you are just a hollow suit of armor!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.41,0:16:44.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.29,0:17:00.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By joining your hands together, you create a ring\Nand then transmute with\Npower that circulates within.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.97,0:17:04.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Without this miserable right hand, you cannot transmute.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.47,0:17:07.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will have to destroy it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.73,0:17:19.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.57,0:17:24.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, run! Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.41,0:17:25.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.66,0:17:31.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will give you a moment\Nto pray to God.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.21,0:17:36.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Unfortunately,\NI've stopped believing in God.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.63,0:17:42.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You said your older brother died in Ishbal, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.97,0:17:46.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was killed...\Nby a State Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.68,0:17:51.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm an older brother too.\NKill me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.43,0:17:52.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It'll be an equivalent exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.23,0:17:54.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about, Brother?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.90,0:17:57.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You said yourself that it wouldn't be an equivalent exchange, didn't you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.02,0:18:00.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's not a State Alchemist!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.94,0:18:03.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I should be enough alone, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.53,0:18:07.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I promise you, I will not go after your brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.03,0:18:12.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, you are wrong, Fullmetal Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.79,0:18:18.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is nothing that can be equivalently exchanged
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.79,0:18:19.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,for the despair over losing \Nyour brother and your people.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.38,0:18:23.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If not, then what is\Nyour vengeance for?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.30,0:18:30.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother! What are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.47,0:18:35.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Get out of there!\NGet up and run!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.02,0:18:39.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.48,0:18:41.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.32,0:18:48.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.57,0:18:52.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You dumb bastard,\Nhaven't you run away?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.33,0:18:55.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I investigated some ancient records once in Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.04,0:18:59.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In them, I saw the design\Nyou have drawn on your right arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.17,0:19:03.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This may be a dud, but it is still a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.13,0:19:05.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And sure enough, your arm is...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.88,0:19:07.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop! Don't say it!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.51,0:19:09.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.22,0:19:12.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san, is this different from when you were using the Stone's power?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.63,0:19:48.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The sewers, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.93,0:19:51.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't go after him.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.84,0:19:51.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not going to!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.76,0:19:52.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yo!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.01,0:19:53.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is it over?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.93,0:19:55.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As long as you're here,\Nyou could at least help us out!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.89,0:19:56.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lay off!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.06,0:20:02.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't go dragging a normal person like me into you ridiculous folks' freak show!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.53,0:20:08.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.53,0:20:09.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hawkeye, take crowd control.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.99,0:20:11.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't let anyone come near.\NRight!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.37,0:20:15.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.54,0:20:17.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You...\Nstupid brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.41,0:20:19.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What was that for?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.58,0:20:21.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why didn't you leave me\Nand run away?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.00,0:20:23.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then you would've been killed!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.00,0:20:27.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So you decide to go and die instead? You idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.21,0:20:29.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't you call your\Nolder brother an idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.26,0:20:31.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll call you that\Nas often as I want!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.84,0:20:36.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Live on, live on, survive,\Nand research more alchemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.47,0:20:38.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so that one day,\Nwe'll get our bodies back.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.06,0:20:42.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dying... Dying by yourself...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.94,0:20:44.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is one thing that\NI absolutely will not allow!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.07,0:20:53.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look, now my arm has \Nbroken off, you moron!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.95,0:20:57.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're falling apart, aren't we?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.70,0:20:59.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We must look just terrible.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.29,0:21:03.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But we're alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.42,0:21:06.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh-huh, alive...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.80,0:21:10.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That suit of armor...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.76,0:21:13.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've never heard of\Na soul transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.51,0:21:16.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He must've risked his life to take on that transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.47,0:21:18.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why the bond between\Nthose two brothers is so strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.06,0:21:20.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.52,0:21:22.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's the Führer's secretary.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.39,0:21:24.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer's secretary?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.90,0:21:28.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer says that we will be taking custody of Marcoh
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.90,0:21:31.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that he will not\Ncome to harm.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.70,0:21:33.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.61,0:21:33.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.66,0:21:35.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.99,0:21:41.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's like I told you, Edward-kun.\NI cannot go to your hometown.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.25,0:21:42.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.79,0:21:45.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The doctor couple who died on the battlefield...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.08,0:21:47.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Their names were Rockbell.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.48,0:22:03.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's be going.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.03,0:22:13.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother,\NI just heard Mom's voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.24,0:22:15.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dummy, you just had a brush with death.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.49,0:22:18.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't start having unstable dreams, now.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.45,0:23:40.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.11,0:23:42.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 16: "That Which Is Lost"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.08,0:23:47.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother's arm and leg...\NMy body...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.12,0:23:52.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In exchange for having lost them,\Nhave we obtained anything?
